<title>UK: SmithKline falls after UBS downgrades stock.</title>
<headline>SmithKline falls after UBS downgrades stock.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in SmithKline Beecham fell to a two-week low on Monday after UBS downgraded the stock to a &quot;hold&quot; from a &quot;buy,&quot; traders said.</p>
<p>By 0839 GMT, the shares were off 12p to 783-1/2p on heavy volume of 1.9 million.  </p>
<p>UBS pharmaceutical analyst Mark Clark said the downgrade was based on performance and valuation, adding that he did not reduce his forecast for the company.</p>
<p>--Debra Sherman, London newsroom +44 171 542 4026</p>
</text>
